{
  "rule_id": "madd_sila_sughra_ha",
  "version": "1",
  "name_ar": "الصلة الصغرى في هاء الضمير",
  "definition": "A pronoun ha between two vowelled letters is lengthened with a waw or yeh of two harakat when no hamza follows.",
  "riwaya": "qaloun",
  "tariq": "unspecified",
  "family": "madd",
  "detectability": "A",
  "limitations": [
    "Paraphrase of the cited pages by an automated drafter; not scholarly reviewed.",
    "Only Book A is cited; the printed page is where the section begins and needs proofreading.",
    "The corpus marks the lengthening itself, so this follows that mark; dropped at a stop.",
    "Book A p.19 item 7 reads فألقه with kasra and sila, while p.20 reads it with kasra and no sila. The rule `madd_sila_ha_exception` lists both readings and chooses none.",
    "Second citation: the longer book Nabhan, which Book A digests. It agrees with the paraphrase, so it shows where the text is found, not an independent confirmation."
  ],
